# Hand-written signatures for the slice of the framework this gem touches.
#
# ## Why this file exists
#
# There are no maintained RBS signatures for Rails, ActionMailer, ActionPack or `mail`, and
# `gem_rbs_collection` does not carry them. Without declarations, `rbs validate` fails on the first
# unknown constant (`::Rails::Railtie` as a superclass) and `steep check` cannot resolve any
# framework call. Generating signatures with `rbs prototype rt` would produce tens of thousands of
# lines of unmaintainable noise, most of it `untyped` anyway.
#
# ## What it deliberately is not
#
# **A slice, not a model of Rails.** It declares exactly the constants and methods `lib/` names, at
# the shallowest fidelity that still type-checks. Framework objects this gem only passes through —
# `Mail::Message`, the request, the config — stay `untyped` on purpose: pretending to model
# `Mail::Message` would be a large second source of truth about somebody else's API, and it would
# be wrong in ways nothing here could detect.
#
# So Steep is not checking the framework calls. What it IS checking, and what the gate is for, is
# this gem's calls INTO THE SDK, which is fully typed and shipped with signatures — the argument
# names and types the delivery method passes to `emails.send`, and what `Webhooks.verify` returns.
# That is the boundary that breaks silently when the SDK moves, and it is the one under test.
#
# ## Not shipped
#
# The gemspec excludes `sig/vendor/` from `spec.files`. Publishing partial Rails signatures would
# put them on the load path of anyone who types this gem, competing with whatever real signatures
# they use, and RBS has no way to know theirs should win.
module Rails
  def self.application: () -> untyped

  class Railtie
    def self.config: () -> untyped
    def self.initializer: (String, **untyped) ?{ (?untyped) -> void } -> void
  end
end

module ActiveSupport
  def self.on_load: (Symbol, **untyped) { (?untyped) [self: untyped] -> void } -> void

  class OrderedOptions
    def []: (Symbol) -> untyped
    def []=: (Symbol, untyped) -> untyped
    def method_missing: (Symbol, *untyped) -> untyped
  end

  module Notifications
    def self.instrument: (String, ?Hash[Symbol, untyped]) ?{ (?untyped) -> void } -> untyped
  end
end

module ActionController
  class Base
    def self.skip_forgery_protection: (**untyped) -> void

    def request: () -> untyped
    def head: (Symbol | Integer, **untyped) -> void
  end
end

module Mail
  class Address
    def format: () -> String
  end
end
